{"paragraphs":[{"text":"%md\n# Ref. '5.5 Dataeksport Spark → Cassandra' in report.\n## Shaping DataFrames to Fit Cassandra Tables\n___\n**Note**  \nThis notebook is part of a collections which has to be run in the following order to work as intended:\n1. [1_Capstone_CQL_DB_Build.zpln](https://github.com/AndreasIsaksen/BD_project_appendices_gruppe1/tree/zpln/zpln/final/Capstone)\n2. [2_Capstone_Frame_to_Table.zpln](https://github.com/AndreasIsaksen/BD_project_appendices_gruppe1/tree/zpln/zpln/final/Capstone)\n3. [3_Capstone_Cassandra_Queries.zpln](https://github.com/AndreasIsaksen/BD_project_appendices_gruppe1/tree/zpln/zpln/final/Capstone)\n___\nThis notebook covers the processing of **spark** dataframes which get designed to fit the different **Cassandra** tables that's being built in accordance to our hypothesises and queries in regards to the **capstone** project.  \n\nThe content in this notebook can be run several times without affecting the content of the tables as long as det source **CSV** data files remains consistent. This is possible since alle export jobs are set to **append** the exported data, which will only add rows of data to the created tables that doesn't already exists within the respective table.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2025-12-12T00:35:26+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h1>Ref. &lsquo;5.5 Dataeksport Spark → Cassandra&rsquo; in report.</h1>\n<h2>Shaping DataFrames to Fit Cassandra Tables</h2>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Note</strong><br />\nThis notebook is part of a collections which has to be run in the following order to work as intended:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/AndreasIsaksen/BD_project_appendices_gruppe1/tree/zpln/zpln/final/Capstone\">1_Capstone_CQL_DB_Build.zpln</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/AndreasIsaksen/BD_project_appendices_gruppe1/tree/zpln/zpln/final/Capstone\">2_Capstone_Frame_to_Table.zpln</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/AndreasIsaksen/BD_project_appendices_gruppe1/tree/zpln/zpln/final/Capstone\">3_Capstone_Cassandra_Queries.zpln</a></li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<p>This notebook covers the processing of <strong>spark</strong> dataframes which get designed to fit the different <strong>Cassandra</strong> tables that&rsquo;s being built in accordance to our hypothesises and queries in regards to the <strong>capstone</strong> project.</p>\n<p>The content in this notebook can be run several times without affecting the content of the tables as long as det source <strong>CSV</strong> data files remains consistent. This is possible since alle export jobs are set to <strong>append</strong> the exported data, which will only add rows of data to the created tables that doesn&rsquo;t already exists within the respective table.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1765482468802_378254801","id":"paragraph_1763574833091_1715575824","dateCreated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","status":"FINISHED","focus":true,"dateFinished":"2025-12-12T00:35:26+0000","dateStarted":"2025-12-12T00:35:26+0000"},{"text":"%md\n## Ref. ‘4. Utforsking og Validering av Prosjektemnet’ in report.\n### Compact Complete Main DataFrame Build.\nThe cell below contains a compact version of the completed dataframe, which is being used to create sub dataframes formed for their respective **Cassandra** tables before frame to table export. Detailed content of this cell can be found in chapter 4 in the report and in [CapstoneData_FrameHandeling.zpln](https://github.com/AndreasIsaksen/BD_project_appendices_gruppe1/tree/zpln/zpln/final/Capstone).","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2025-12-12T01:36:30+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h2>Ref. ‘4. Utforsking og Validering av Prosjektemnet’ in report.</h2>\n<h3>Compact Complete Main DataFrame Build.</h3>\n<p>The cell below contains a compact version of the completed dataframe, which is being used to create sub dataframes formed for their respective <strong>Cassandra</strong> tables before frame to table export. Detailed content of this cell can be found in chapter 4 in the report and in <a href=\"https://github.com/AndreasIsaksen/BD_project_appendices_gruppe1/tree/zpln/zpln/final/Capstone\">CapstoneData_FrameHandeling.zpln</a>.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1765482468803_715584094","id":"paragraph_1763580823452_1363074591","dateCreated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","status":"FINISHED","dateFinished":"2025-12-12T01:36:30+0000","dateStarted":"2025-12-12T01:36:30+0000"},{"text":"%spark\r\n// Package import\r\nimport spark.implicits._\r\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.types._\r\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.expressions._\r\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.functions._\r\n\r\n// Sett timezone to NO\r\nspark.conf.set(\"spark.sql.session.timeZone\", \"Europe/Oslo\")\r\n\r\n// Source paths\r\nval bil_base = \"/sparkio/trafikkdata/bil/*.csv\"\r\nval sykkel_base = \"/sparkio/trafikkdata/sykkel/*.csv\"\r\nval weather_base = \"/sparkio/værdata/*.csv\"\r\n\r\n// Defining Schemas\r\nval trafikk_Schema = StructType(Array(\r\n    StructField(\"trafikkregistreringspunkt\", StringType, true),\r\n\tStructField(\"navn\", StringType, true),\r\n\tStructField(\"vegreferanse\", StringType, true),\r\n\tStructField(\"fra\", TimestampType, true),\r\n\tStructField(\"til\", TimestampType, true),\r\n\tStructField(\"dato\", DateType, true),\r\n\tStructField(\"fra tidspunkt\", StringType, true),\r\n\tStructField(\"til tidspunkt\", StringType, true),\r\n\tStructField(\"felt\", StringType, true),\r\n\tStructField(\"trafikkmengde\", ShortType, true),\r\n\tStructField(\"dekningsgrad (%)\", StringType, true),\r\n\tStructField(\"antall timer total\", ByteType, true),\r\n\tStructField(\"antall timer inkludert\", ByteType, true),\r\n\tStructField(\"antall timer ugyldig\", ByteType, true),\r\n\tStructField(\"ikke gyldig lengde\", ByteType, true),\r\n\tStructField(\"lengdekvalitetsgrad (%)\", StringType, true),\r\n\tStructField(\"< 5,6m\", ShortType, true),\r\n\tStructField(\">= 5,6m\", ShortType, true),\r\n\tStructField(\"5,6m - 7,6m\", ShortType, true),\r\n\tStructField(\"7,6m - 12,5m\", ShortType, true),\r\n\tStructField(\"12,5m - 16,0m\", ShortType, true),\r\n\tStructField(\">= 16,0m\", ShortType, true),\r\n\tStructField(\"16,0m - 24,0m\", ShortType, true),\r\n\tStructField(\">= 24,0m\", ShortType, true)\r\n))\r\n\r\nval weather_Schema = StructType(Array(\r\n    StructField(\"navn\", StringType, true),\r\n\tStructField(\"stasjon\", StringType, true),\r\n\tStructField(\"tid(norsk normaltid)\", TimestampType, true),\r\n\tStructField(\"nedbør (1 t)\", StringType, true),\r\n\tStructField(\"lufttemperatur\", StringType, true),\r\n    StructField(\"Antall minutter nedbør siste time\", StringType, true),\r\n\tStructField(\"høyeste middelvind (1 t)\", StringType, true)\r\n))\r\n\r\n// Data import\r\nval bil_raw_df = spark.read\r\n    .option(\"header\", true)\r\n    .option(\"recursiveFileLookup\", true)\r\n    .schema(trafikk_Schema)\r\n    .option(\"delimiter\", \";\")\r\n    .option(\"nullValue\", \"-\")\r\n    .option(\"timestampFormat\", \"yyyy-MM-dd'T'HH:mmXXX\")    \r\n    .csv(bil_base)\r\n\r\nval sykkel_raw_df = spark.read\r\n    .option(\"header\", true)\r\n    .option(\"recursiveFileLookup\", true)\r\n    .schema(trafikk_Schema)\r\n    .option(\"delimiter\", \";\")\r\n    .option(\"nullValue\", \"-\")\r\n    .option(\"timestampFormat\", \"yyyy-MM-dd'T'HH:mmXXX\")    \r\n    .csv(sykkel_base)\r\n\r\nval weather_raw_df = spark.read\r\n    .option(\"header\", true)\r\n    .option(\"recursiveFileLookup\", true)\r\n    .schema(weather_Schema)\r\n    .option(\"delimiter\", \";\")\r\n    .option(\"nullValue\", \"-\")\r\n    .option(\"timestampFormat\", \"dd.MM.yyyy HH:mm\")\r\n    .csv(weather_base)\r\n\r\n// Data handeling\r\nval bil_rm_dup = bil_raw_df.dropDuplicates()\r\nval sykkel_rm_dup = sykkel_raw_df.dropDuplicates()\r\nval weather_rm_dup = weather_raw_df.dropDuplicates()\r\n\r\nval bil_raw = bil_rm_dup.withColumn(\"klasse\", lit(0).cast(ByteType))\r\nval sykkel_raw = sykkel_rm_dup.withColumn(\"klasse\", lit(1).cast(ByteType))\r\nval trafikk_raw_df = bil_raw.union(sykkel_raw)\r\n\r\nval trafikk_df_formatFix = trafikk_raw_df\r\n    .withColumn(\r\n        \"dekningsgrad (%)\",\r\n        replace(col(\"dekningsgrad (%)\"), lit(\",\"), lit(\".\")).cast(FloatType)\r\n    )\r\n    .withColumn(\r\n        \"lengdekvalitetsgrad (%)\",\r\n        replace(col(\"lengdekvalitetsgrad (%)\"), lit(\",\"), lit(\".\")).cast(FloatType)\r\n    )\r\n    .withColumn(\r\n        \"navn\",\r\n        trim(replace(col(\"navn\"), lit(\" sykkeltavle mot metrering\"), lit(\"\")))\r\n    )\r\n    .withColumn(\r\n        \"navn\",\r\n        trim(replace(col(\"navn\"), lit(\" sykkel\"), lit(\"\")))\r\n    )\r\n    .withColumn(\r\n        \"fra tidspunkt\",\r\n        date_format(col(\"fra\"), \"k\").cast(\"byte\")\r\n    )\r\n    .withColumn(\r\n        \"til tidspunkt\",\r\n        date_format(col(\"til\"), \"k\").cast(\"byte\")\r\n    )\r\n\r\nval weather_df_formatfix = weather_rm_dup\r\n    .withColumn(\r\n        \"nedbør (1 t)\",\r\n        replace(col(\"nedbør (1 t)\"), lit(\",\"), lit(\".\")).cast(FloatType)\r\n    )\r\n    .withColumn(\r\n        \"lufttemperatur\",\r\n        replace(col(\"lufttemperatur\"), lit(\",\"), lit(\".\")).cast(FloatType)\r\n    )\r\n    .withColumn(\r\n        \"høyeste middelvind (1 t)\",\r\n        replace(col(\"høyeste middelvind (1 t)\"), lit(\",\"), lit(\".\")).cast(FloatType)\r\n    )\r\n\r\nval complete_df_raw = trafikk_df_formatFix.alias(\"c\")\r\n    .join(weather_df_formatfix.alias(\"w\"),\r\n        col(\"c.fra\") === col(\"w.tid(norsk normaltid)\"),\"cross\")\r\n    .select(\r\n        col(\"c.*\"),\r\n        col(\"w.lufttemperatur\"),\r\n        col(\"w.høyeste middelvind (1 t)\").as(\"høyeste middelvind (m/s)\")\r\n    )\r\n\r\nval validation = complete_df_raw\r\n    .filter( ! (col(\"dekningsgrad (%)\") === 0 && col(\"trafikkmengde\").isNotNull))\r\n\r\nval validated_df = validation\r\n    .filter( ! (col(\"Lengdekvalitetsgrad (%)\") === 0 && col(\"trafikkmengde\").isNotNull && col(\"klasse\") === 0))\r\n\r\nval complete_df = validated_df\r\n    .withColumn(\"ukedag\", date_format(col(\"dato\"), \"EEE\"))","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2025-12-12T01:36:23+0000","progress":0,"config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"import spark.implicits._\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.types._\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.expressions._\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.functions._\n\u001b[1m\u001b[34mbil_base\u001b[0m: \u001b[1m\u001b[32mString\u001b[0m = /sparkio/trafikkdata/bil/*.csv\n\u001b[1m\u001b[34msykkel_base\u001b[0m: \u001b[1m\u001b[32mString\u001b[0m = /sparkio/trafikkdata/sykkel/*.csv\n\u001b[1m\u001b[34mweather_base\u001b[0m: \u001b[1m\u001b[32mString\u001b[0m = /sparkio/værdata/*.csv\n\u001b[1m\u001b[34mtrafikk_Schema\u001b[0m: \u001b[1m\u001b[32morg.apache.spark.sql.types.StructType\u001b[0m = StructType(StructField(trafikkregistreringspunkt,StringType,true),StructField(navn,StringType,true),StructField(vegreferanse,StringType,true),StructField(fra,TimestampType,true),StructField(til,TimestampType,true),StructField(dato,DateType,true),StructField(fra tidspunkt,StringType,true),StructField(til tidspunkt,StringType,true),StructFiel...\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1765482468803_990433809","id":"paragraph_1762894782944_1826176745","dateCreated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","status":"FINISHED","focus":false,"dateFinished":"2025-12-12T01:30:49+0000","dateStarted":"2025-12-12T01:30:42+0000"},{"text":"%md\n## Ref. ‘5.5 Dataeksport Spark → Cassandra’ in report.\n### Sub DataFrames and transfer from **spark** to **Cassandra**\nThe following cells contains jobs that shape sub-dataframes from the 'complete_df' dataframe to fit their respective **Cassandra Tables** (found in [1_Capstone_CQL_DB_Build.zpln](https://github.com/AndreasIsaksen/BD_project_appendices_gruppe1/tree/zpln/zpln/final/Capstone)), before the subframe is tranfered to a table.  \nEach cell contains the creation of a subframe and transfer job to the given table.  ","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h2>Ref. ‘5.5 Dataeksport Spark → Cassandra’ in report.</h2>\n<h3>Sub DataFrames and transfer from <strong>spark</strong> to <strong>Cassandra</strong></h3>\n<p>The following cells contains jobs that shape sub-dataframes from the &lsquo;complete_df&rsquo; dataframe to fit their respective <strong>Cassandra Tables</strong> (found in <a href=\"https://github.com/AndreasIsaksen/BD_project_appendices_gruppe1/tree/zpln/zpln/final/Capstone\">1_Capstone_CQL_DB_Build.zpln</a>), before the subframe is tranfered to a table.<br />\nEach cell contains the creation of a subframe and transfer job to the given table.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1765482468803_582798885","id":"paragraph_1763125666859_1497475691","dateCreated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","status":"READY"},{"text":"%md\n### Hypothesis 1\nDen totale trafikkmengden inn og ut av Fredrikstad gjennom én time er høyest i rushtiden hverdager mellom 15 : 00 og 16 : 00.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h3>Hypothesis 1</h3>\n<p>Den totale trafikkmengden inn og ut av Fredrikstad gjennom én time er høyest i rushtiden hverdager mellom 15 : 00 og 16 : 00.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1765482468804_1177089098","id":"paragraph_1763584680057_2016530155","dateCreated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","status":"READY"},{"text":"%md\n#### Description\nTo export the relevant data for the corresponding table in *Cassandra*, a new *DataFrame* named **df_rushtid** is created.\nThis DataFrame contains only the columns required by the table’s design.\nBefore exporting the data, rows where **trafikkmengde** is null are filtered out, as these entries are not relevant for the analysis.\nAdditionally, rows where **felt** equals **'Totalt'** are retained, since only the total traffic volume is of interest for this hypothesis. This prevents potential duplicate traffic measurements from separate lanes on the roadway.\nRows corresponding to weekends (Saturday and Sunday) are also removed, as the hypothesis concerns only weekdays.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h4>Description</h4>\n<p>To export the relevant data for the corresponding table in <em>Cassandra</em>, a new <em>DataFrame</em> named <strong>df_rushtid</strong> is created.<br />\nThis DataFrame contains only the columns required by the table’s design.<br />\nBefore exporting the data, rows where <strong>trafikkmengde</strong> is null are filtered out, as these entries are not relevant for the analysis.<br />\nAdditionally, rows where <strong>felt</strong> equals <strong>&lsquo;Totalt&rsquo;</strong> are retained, since only the total traffic volume is of interest for this hypothesis. This prevents potential duplicate traffic measurements from separate lanes on the roadway.<br />\nRows corresponding to weekends (Saturday and Sunday) are also removed, as the hypothesis concerns only weekdays.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1765482468804_2137555335","id":"paragraph_1763975137165_940273192","dateCreated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","status":"READY"},{"text":"%spark\nval df_rushtid = complete_df\n    .select(\n        col(\"navn\"),\n        col(\"dato\"),\n        col(\"ukedag\"),\n        col(\"fra tidspunkt\"),\n        col(\"til tidspunkt\"),\n        col(\"trafikkmengde\")\n    )\n    .filter(!(col(\"trafikkmengde\").isNull))\n    .filter(col(\"felt\") === \"Totalt\")\n    .filter(!col(\"ukedag\").contains(\"Saturday\"))\n    .filter(!col(\"ukedag\").contains(\"Sunday\"))\n    .withColumnRenamed(\"fra tidspunkt\", \"fra\")\n    .withColumnRenamed(\"til tidspunkt\", \"til\")\n    \ndf_rushtid.write\n    .format(\"org.apache.spark.sql.cassandra\")\n    .options(Map(\n        \"table\" -> \"rushtid\",\n        \"keyspace\" -> \"capstone_ks\"\n    ))\n    .mode(\"append\")\n    .save()","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","progress":0,"config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"\u001b[1m\u001b[34mdf_rushtid\u001b[0m: \u001b[1m\u001b[32morg.apache.spark.sql.DataFrame\u001b[0m = [navn: string, dato: date ... 4 more fields]\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1765482468804_1509347551","id":"paragraph_1763311358771_360721402","dateCreated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","status":"READY"},{"text":"%md\n### Hypothesis 2\nDen totale trafikkmengden inn og ut av Fredrikstad er lavere i juli måned enn for resten av året.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h3>Hypothesis 2</h3>\n<p>Den totale trafikkmengden inn og ut av Fredrikstad er lavere i juli måned enn for resten av året.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1765482468804_1397195943","id":"paragraph_1763585064212_598477323","dateCreated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","status":"READY"},{"text":"%md\n#### Description\nThe *DataFrame* **df_trafikkmengde_mnd** is created to contain the columns relevant for the corresponding table in *Cassandra*.\nBefore exporting, rows where **trafikkmengde** is null are filtered out, as these entries are not relevant for the analysis.\nAdditionally, rows where **felt** equals **'Totalt'** are retained, since only the total traffic volume is of interest for this hypothesis. This prevents potential duplicate measurements resulting from separate lane-specific counts.\nTwo new columns, **mnd** and **yr**, are then created by extracting the month and year components from the **dato** column. These columns are converted to numeric types to match the table’s design and to simplify future filtering in queries.\nThe data is then grouped by **yr**, **mnd**, and **navn**, with **trafikkmengde** aggregated by summing the values within each group. Finally, the result is sorted by **yr** and **mnd** to ensure chronological order during export.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h4>Description</h4>\n<p>The <em>DataFrame</em> <strong>df_trafikkmengde_mnd</strong> is created to contain the columns relevant for the corresponding table in <em>Cassandra</em>.<br />\nBefore exporting, rows where <strong>trafikkmengde</strong> is null are filtered out, as these entries are not relevant for the analysis.<br />\nAdditionally, rows where <strong>felt</strong> equals <strong>&lsquo;Totalt&rsquo;</strong> are retained, since only the total traffic volume is of interest for this hypothesis. This prevents potential duplicate measurements resulting from separate lane-specific counts.<br />\nTwo new columns, <strong>mnd</strong> and <strong>yr</strong>, are then created by extracting the month and year components from the <strong>dato</strong> column. These columns are converted to numeric types to match the table’s design and to simplify future filtering in queries.<br />\nThe data is then grouped by <strong>yr</strong>, <strong>mnd</strong>, and <strong>navn</strong>, with <strong>trafikkmengde</strong> aggregated by summing the values within each group. Finally, the result is sorted by <strong>yr</strong> and <strong>mnd</strong> to ensure chronological order during export.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1765482468804_1831090820","id":"paragraph_1763975180474_1853204254","dateCreated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","status":"READY"},{"text":"%spark\nval df_trafikkmengde_mnd = complete_df\n    .select(\n        col(\"navn\"),\n        col(\"dato\"),\n        col(\"ukedag\"),\n        col(\"trafikkmengde\")\n    )\n    .filter(col(\"trafikkmengde\").isNotNull)\n    .filter(col(\"felt\") === \"Totalt\")\n    .withColumn(\"mnd\", month(col(\"dato\")).cast(\"byte\"))\n    .withColumn(\"yr\", date_format(col(\"dato\"), \"yyyy\").cast(\"int\"))\n    .groupBy(\"yr\", \"mnd\", \"navn\")\n    .agg(sum(col(\"trafikkmengde\")).as(\"trafikkmengde\"))\n    .orderBy(\"yr\", \"mnd\")\n\ndf_trafikkmengde_mnd.write\n    .format(\"org.apache.spark.sql.cassandra\")\n    .options(Map(\n        \"table\" -> \"trafikkmengde_mnd\",\n        \"keyspace\" -> \"capstone_ks\"\n    ))\n    .mode(\"append\")\n    .save()","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","progress":0,"config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"\u001b[1m\u001b[34mdf_trafikkmengde_mnd\u001b[0m: \u001b[1m\u001b[32morg.apache.spark.sql.Dataset[org.apache.spark.sql.Row]\u001b[0m = [yr: int, mnd: tinyint ... 2 more fields]\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1765482468805_1109859711","id":"paragraph_1763316236415_776999641","dateCreated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","status":"READY"},{"text":"%md\n### Hypothesis 3\nDet finnes en positiv korrelasjon for temperatur og total sykkeltrafikk i Fredrikstad målt over en referanseperiode mellom 10 : 00 − 14 : 00.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h3>Hypothesis 3</h3>\n<p>Det finnes en positiv korrelasjon for temperatur og total sykkeltrafikk i Fredrikstad målt over en referanseperiode mellom 10 : 00 − 14 : 00.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1765482468805_1282629729","id":"paragraph_1763585375432_887023038","dateCreated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","status":"READY"},{"text":"%md\n#### Description\nThe *DataFrame* **df_sykkel_temp_corr** is created to contain the columns relevant for the corresponding table in *Cassandra*.\nBefore export, rows where **trafikkmengde** is null are filtered out, as these entries are not relevant for the analysis.\nAdditionally, rows where **felt** equals **'Totalt'** are retained, since only the total traffic volume is of interest for this hypothesis. This prevents potential duplicate measurements caused by separate lane-specific counts.\nThe data is further filtered to include only rows where **klasse** equals *1*, which represents bicycle traffic in the dataset.\nNext, two new columns, **fra** and **til**, are created by extracting the values from the **fra tidspunkt** and **til tidspunkt** columns, which contain numeric values representing hourly timestamps.\nTo focus on the hypothesis’ reference period, the data is filtered to include rows where **fra** lies between *10* and *13*, representing the time interval from *10:00* to *14:00*. This ensures that all hourly intervals within this daily time range are included, enabling the hypothesis to be evaluated.\nBefore exporting the data, unnecessary columns that are not relevant to the table’s design are removed.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h4>Description</h4>\n<p>The <em>DataFrame</em> <strong>df_sykkel_temp_corr</strong> is created to contain the columns relevant for the corresponding table in <em>Cassandra</em>.<br />\nBefore export, rows where <strong>trafikkmengde</strong> is null are filtered out, as these entries are not relevant for the analysis.<br />\nAdditionally, rows where <strong>felt</strong> equals <strong>&lsquo;Totalt&rsquo;</strong> are retained, since only the total traffic volume is of interest for this hypothesis. This prevents potential duplicate measurements caused by separate lane-specific counts.<br />\nThe data is further filtered to include only rows where <strong>klasse</strong> equals <em>1</em>, which represents bicycle traffic in the dataset.<br />\nNext, two new columns, <strong>fra</strong> and <strong>til</strong>, are created by extracting the values from the <strong>fra tidspunkt</strong> and <strong>til tidspunkt</strong> columns, which contain numeric values representing hourly timestamps.<br />\nTo focus on the hypothesis’ reference period, the data is filtered to include rows where <strong>fra</strong> lies between <em>10</em> and <em>13</em>, representing the time interval from <em>10:00</em> to <em>14:00</em>. This ensures that all hourly intervals within this daily time range are included, enabling the hypothesis to be evaluated.<br />\nBefore exporting the data, unnecessary columns that are not relevant to the table’s design are removed.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1765482468805_1443886306","id":"paragraph_1763975184704_106706806","dateCreated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","status":"READY"},{"text":"%spark\nval df_sykkel_temp_corr = complete_df.select(\"navn\", \"dato\", \"klasse\", \"fra tidspunkt\", \"til tidspunkt\", \"felt\", \"trafikkmengde\", \"lufttemperatur\")\n    .filter(!(col(\"trafikkmengde\").isNull))\n    .filter(col(\"felt\") === \"Totalt\")\n    .filter(col(\"klasse\") === 1)\n    .withColumnRenamed(\"til tidspunkt\", \"til\")\n    .withColumnRenamed(\"fra tidspunkt\", \"fra\")\n    .filter(col(\"fra\").between(10,13))\n    .drop(col(\"felt\"))\n    .drop(col(\"klasse\"))\n    .drop(col(\"fra tidspunkt\"))\n    .drop(col(\"til tidspunkt\"))\n\ndf_sykkel_temp_corr.write\n    .format(\"org.apache.spark.sql.cassandra\")\n    .options(Map(\n        \"table\" -> \"sykkel_temp_corr\",\n        \"keyspace\" -> \"capstone_ks\"\n    ))\n    .mode(\"append\")\n    .save()","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","progress":0,"config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionSupport":true,"completionKey":"TAB"},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"\u001b[1m\u001b[34mdf_sykkel_temp_corr\u001b[0m: \u001b[1m\u001b[32morg.apache.spark.sql.DataFrame\u001b[0m = [navn: string, dato: date ... 4 more fields]\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1765482468806_37764778","id":"paragraph_1763585445379_1274510823","dateCreated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","status":"READY"},{"text":"%md\n### Hypothesis 4\nDet finnes en negativ korrelasjon for temperatur og total biltrafikk i Fredrikstad målt over en referanseperiode mellom 10 : 00 − 14 : 00.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h3>Hypothesis 4</h3>\n<p>Det finnes en negativ korrelasjon for temperatur og total biltrafikk i Fredrikstad målt over en referanseperiode mellom 10 : 00 − 14 : 00.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1765482468806_2005711992","id":"paragraph_1763585466362_2123422967","dateCreated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","status":"READY"},{"text":"%md\n#### Description\nThis *DataFrame* has the same structure and purpose as **df_sykkel_temp_corr** from Hypothesis 3, but it is designed to extract car traffic data.\nFirst, the relevant columns for the table’s design are selected.\nRows where **trafikkmengde** is null are then filtered out, as these entries are not relevant for the analysis.\nAdditionally, rows where **felt** equals **'Totalt'** are retained, since only the total traffic volume is of interest for this hypothesis. This prevents potential duplicate measurements caused by lane-specific counts.\nThe data is further filtered to include only rows where **klasse** equals *0*, which represents car traffic in the dataset.\nNext, two new columns, **fra** and **til**, are created by extracting the values from the **fra tidspunkt** and **til tidspunkt** columns, which contain numeric hour-based timestamps.\nTo focus on the hypothesis’ reference period, the data is filtered to include rows where **fra** lies between *10* and *13*, representing the time interval from *10:00* to *14:00*. This ensures that all hourly intervals within this daily range are included, enabling the hypothesis to be evaluated.\nBefore exporting the data, unnecessary columns that are not relevant to the table’s design are removed.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h4>Description</h4>\n<p>This <em>DataFrame</em> has the same structure and purpose as <strong>df_sykkel_temp_corr</strong> from Hypothesis 3, but it is designed to extract car traffic data.<br />\nFirst, the relevant columns for the table’s design are selected.<br />\nRows where <strong>trafikkmengde</strong> is null are then filtered out, as these entries are not relevant for the analysis.<br />\nAdditionally, rows where <strong>felt</strong> equals <strong>&lsquo;Totalt&rsquo;</strong> are retained, since only the total traffic volume is of interest for this hypothesis. This prevents potential duplicate measurements caused by lane-specific counts.<br />\nThe data is further filtered to include only rows where <strong>klasse</strong> equals <em>0</em>, which represents car traffic in the dataset.<br />\nNext, two new columns, <strong>fra</strong> and <strong>til</strong>, are created by extracting the values from the <strong>fra tidspunkt</strong> and <strong>til tidspunkt</strong> columns, which contain numeric hour-based timestamps.<br />\nTo focus on the hypothesis’ reference period, the data is filtered to include rows where <strong>fra</strong> lies between <em>10</em> and <em>13</em>, representing the time interval from <em>10:00</em> to <em>14:00</em>. This ensures that all hourly intervals within this daily range are included, enabling the hypothesis to be evaluated.<br />\nBefore exporting the data, unnecessary columns that are not relevant to the table’s design are removed.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1765482468806_1644400671","id":"paragraph_1763975188975_2013797814","dateCreated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","status":"READY"},{"text":"%spark\nval df_bil_temp_corr = complete_df.select(\"navn\", \"dato\", \"klasse\", \"fra tidspunkt\", \"til tidspunkt\", \"felt\", \"trafikkmengde\", \"lufttemperatur\")\n    .filter(!(col(\"trafikkmengde\").isNull))\n    .filter(col(\"felt\") === \"Totalt\")\n    .filter(col(\"klasse\") === 0)\n    .withColumnRenamed(\"til tidspunkt\", \"til\")\n    .withColumnRenamed(\"fra tidspunkt\", \"fra\")\n    .filter(col(\"fra\").between(10,13))\n    .drop(col(\"felt\"))\n    .drop(col(\"klasse\"))\n    .drop(col(\"fra tidspunkt\"))\n    .drop(col(\"til tidspunkt\"))\n\ndf_bil_temp_corr.write\n    .format(\"org.apache.spark.sql.cassandra\")\n    .options(Map(\n        \"table\" -> \"bil_temp_corr\",\n        \"keyspace\" -> \"capstone_ks\"\n    ))\n    .mode(\"append\")\n    .save()","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","progress":0,"config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionSupport":true,"completionKey":"TAB"},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"\u001b[1m\u001b[34mdf_bil_temp_corr\u001b[0m: \u001b[1m\u001b[32morg.apache.spark.sql.DataFrame\u001b[0m = [navn: string, dato: date ... 4 more fields]\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1765482468807_1890066873","id":"paragraph_1763585482893_909138166","dateCreated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","status":"READY"},{"text":"%md\n### Hypothesis 5\nData kan benyttes til å forutsi om det er blitt utført veiarbeid eller vedlikehold på et gitt trafikk registreringspunkt basert på uregelmessigheter i trafikkmålinger","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h3>Hypothesis 5</h3>\n<p>Data kan benyttes til å forutsi om det er blitt utført veiarbeid eller vedlikehold på et gitt trafikk registreringspunkt basert på uregelmessigheter i trafikkmålinger</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1765482468807_417186636","id":"paragraph_1763585529184_1658240483","dateCreated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","status":"READY"},{"text":"%md\n#### Description\nSince the final *DataFrame* has already filtered out the rows relevant to this solution, **complete_df_raw** is used for this export instead.\nThis DataFrame contains rows where **dekningsgrad (%)** before they are removed in the final processed DataFrame.\nTo extract the data needed for this hypothesis, a new *DataFrame* is created containing only the columns **navn**, **dato**, and **fra tidspunkt**.\nThe data is then filtered to include only rows where **dekningsgrad (%)} = 0**.\nFinally, this *DataFrame* is exported to the **Cassandra** table **veiarbeid**, which has been defined to sort incoming data by date and time.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h4>Description</h4>\n<p>Since the final <em>DataFrame</em> has already filtered out the rows relevant to this solution, <strong>complete_df_raw</strong> is used for this export instead.<br />\nThis DataFrame contains rows where <strong>dekningsgrad (%)</strong> before they are removed in the final processed DataFrame.<br />\nTo extract the data needed for this hypothesis, a new <em>DataFrame</em> is created containing only the columns <strong>navn</strong>, <strong>dato</strong>, and <strong>fra tidspunkt</strong>.<br />\nThe data is then filtered to include only rows where <strong>dekningsgrad (%)} = 0</strong>.<br />\nFinally, this <em>DataFrame</em> is exported to the <strong>Cassandra</strong> table <strong>veiarbeid</strong>, which has been defined to sort incoming data by date and time.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1765482468807_2119817071","id":"paragraph_1763975193654_1385868029","dateCreated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","status":"READY"},{"text":"%spark\nval df_veiarbeid = complete_df_raw\n    .select(\n        col(\"navn\"),\n        col(\"dato\"),\n        col(\"fra tidspunkt\"),\n    )\n    .withColumnRenamed(\"fra tidspunkt\", \"fra\")\n    .filter(col(\"dekningsgrad (%)\") === 0)\n\ndf_veiarbeid.write\n    .format(\"org.apache.spark.sql.cassandra\")\n    .options(Map(\n        \"table\" -> \"veiarbeid\",\n        \"keyspace\" -> \"capstone_ks\"\n    ))\n    .mode(\"append\")\n    .save()","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","progress":0,"config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"\u001b[1m\u001b[34mdf_veiarbeid\u001b[0m: \u001b[1m\u001b[32morg.apache.spark.sql.Dataset[org.apache.spark.sql.Row]\u001b[0m = [navn: string, dato: date ... 1 more field]\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1765482468807_1438626710","id":"paragraph_1763325050674_2079890444","dateCreated":"2025-12-11T19:47:48+0000","status":"READY"}],"name":"2_Capstone_Frame_to_Table","id":"2MCAHWT4C","defaultInterpreterGroup":"spark","version":"0.12.0","noteParams":{},"noteForms":{},"angularObjects":{},"config":{"isZeppelinNotebookCronEnable":false,"looknfeel":"default","personalizedMode":"false"},"info":{},"path":"/2_Capstone_Frame_to_Table"}